# For Pis running the full Raspberry Pi OS "Desktop" image (LXDE/PIXEL, X11,
# LightDM) rather than OS Lite. LightDM already runs its own X server and
# session -- this file autostarts Chromium *inside* that session instead of
# fighting it for the display, which is what the systemd+xinit path
# (instruction-kiosk.service) would otherwise do.
#
# Copy this to ~/.config/lxsession/LXDE-pi/autostart (creating the directory
# if needed). Note this REPLACES the default autostart list for this user,
# not appends to it -- for a kiosk that's actually what you want, since it
# also suppresses the taskbar/panel and desktop icons that would otherwise
# be visible for a moment before Chromium covers them.

@xset s off
@xset -dpms
@xset s noblank
@/usr/local/bin/instruction-kiosk.sh
